      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I am having this issue as well still. On teleport or portal entry the world will fade to the black screen or barely visible darkness and stay there. No menus can be opened and waiting does not load the world. Only restarting unfreezes it. Repeated attempts at restarting may allow for a coupe of teleports before it freezes on the next teleport attempt. This seems to be able to happen on initial world load up as well as any teleport attempt. The loading bar for said world does not appear, if it happens on login it shows the login bar then fades to black and does not continue from there. On entering a portal it is the same as a regular teleport attempt. The world (That you are in then) fades to black as if it is ready to begin loading the next world, but the loading screen for the next world never comes. (Nvidia graphics card - Oculus rift device - All updated drivers - No files failed to validate on check according to steam - Reinstall did not help)",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
